    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n3016" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ăpĭastrum</span></b> , i,
			n.
		id.. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Wild-parsley</i>: Selinum palustre, Linn.; <i><span class="en">Plin. 21,
				12, 41, § 70</span></i>; cf. <i><span class="en">Col. 9, 8,
				12</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Balm</i>, <i>a plant of which bees are
				fond</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">melissophyllon,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Varr. R. R. 3, 16, 10</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Plin. 21, 9, 29, § 53</span></i>.</div>
